      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing Forest instead of Fabled Passage on turn 1 is suboptimal. With Llanowar Elves to cast this turn and a hand full of landfall synergies (Mossborn Hydra, Sazh's Chocobo, Earthbender Ascension), Fabled Passage would be better played on turn 1 (when it enters tapped anyway since you control fewer than 4 lands) to save the Forest for a later turn where playing Forest + cracking Fabled Passage would give two landfall triggers. Playing Fabled Passage turn 1 also thins the deck. However, since Forest lets them cast Llanowar Elves this turn regardless, the immediate impact is small - the difference is in future landfall sequencing.",
