      "description": "Haiku Valley cast Sazh's Chocobo before playing a land. They have 4 Forests in hand. By playing a Forest first, the new Chocobo would enter before the land drop and miss the landfall trigger, BUT the existing Sazh's Chocobo would get another +1/+1 counter immediately. More importantly, if they play the land first, then cast Chocobo, the Chocobo enters as a 0/1 but the existing Chocobo gets bigger. However, the optimal sequence is: cast Chocobo first (it enters as 0/1), THEN play a Forest to trigger landfall on BOTH Chocobos simultaneously, giving both a +1/+1 counter. Actually, this is exactly what they can still do - cast Chocobo, then play land. So the order here (Chocobo before land) is actually correct for maximizing landfall triggers on both Chocobos. This is not a blunder.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Sazh's Chocobo before playing a land",
      "better_line": "This sequencing is actually correct - cast Chocobo first, then play land to trigger landfall on both Chocobos",
      "type": "blunder",
