      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Sarge is at 11 life and taking 4 damage from an unblocked Sazh's Chocobo (4/5), going to 7 life. The opponent is at 3 life and Gem3F Sarge has two Deep-Cavern Bats (1/1 flyers) that are tapped (presumably attacked this turn or were tapped). However, blocking with Enduring Curiosity (4/3) would trade it into the 4/5 Chocobo - Enduring Curiosity dies but returns as an enchantment (losing its 4/3 body but keeping the card-draw ability). Taking 4 damage when at 11 life against an opponent at 3 life seems acceptable on the surface, but the Chocobo will keep growing with landfall triggers and Earthbender Ascension has 7 quest counters meaning every land drop gives +1/+1 counters and trample. The Chocobo could quickly become lethal. Blocking with Enduring Curiosity to kill the Chocobo (trading a 4/3 body that comes back as an enchantment) would remove the primary threat while preserving the card-draw engine. The opponent's only creature would be gone, and Gem3F Sarge could close the game with flyers against an opponent at 3 life.",
